  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"2a\"><p><strong>2a</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Power radiated by the star per square metre at the position of the planet:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{(1)(5.67 \\times 10^{-8})(4 \\pi \\times (8.2 \\times 10^{9})^{2})(12300)^{4}}{(4 \\pi)(4.1 \\times 10^{12})^{2}} \\approx 5190\"></span> W m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\approx 5200\"></span> W m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span></p>\n<p>Calculated answer must be given to at least 3 significant figures in order to earn the final mark.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"2b\"><p><strong>2b</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Intensity of the radiation that reaches the surface of the planet:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"(5200)(1-0.43) \\approx 2964\"></span> W m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span></p>\n<p>This intensity is spread over the entire surface of the planet, so the average intensity over the entire surface is:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2964}{4} \\approx 741\"></span> W m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"741 = (1)(5.67 \\times 10^{-8}) \\times T^{4}\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T \\approx 340\"></span> K</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The radius of a star is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8.2 \\times 10^{6}\"></span> km and its surface temperature is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"12300\"></span> K. A planet orbits the star in a circular orbit with radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.1 \\times 10^{9}\"></span> km. The albedo of the planet's atmosphere is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.43\"></span>.</p>\n<p>a. Show that the intensity of the radiation at the position of the planet is about <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5200\"></span> W m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>b. Estimate the average surface temperature of the planet. </p>\n<p>  [3]</p>"
  },
